{"baseRefName":"stack/2-publishing-events","baseRefOid":"f5f3ff13ca330ae3c855d43a9b73afd073eacabb","body":"Genie –\r\n\r\n> Closes #401 · Supersedes `NodeSettingsSession` from #396\r\n> \r\n> 3 of 6.\r\n> \r\n> ### What it establishes\r\n> - A node with settings exposes them as one `NodeSettings` value, through `settings` and `apply(_:)`, and offers `init(context:settings:)`. The value is saved flattened under the node's existing keys, so documents are unchanged.\r\n> - `Graph.setSettings` records one step: the settings either side, and the states of the ports the change touched. Wires and proxies register their own steps in the same group.\r\n> - Settings views hold a draft and commit it. Pickers and steppers commit on each change; text and code commit after a pause and when editing ends. Code editors record no typing undo of their own, so the draft is the only record.\r\n> - Every node with settings is migrated: Strategy, Routing, Format String, Math Expression, Parametric Geometry, JavaScript, Live Image, Timeline, the device nodes, the local model nodes and Deferred Render.\r\n> - The Fabric Editor's Undo and Redo go through the root graph, with their menu state cached from notifications.\r\n> \r\n> ### Not in this PR\r\n> - Create Subgraph through the public API, and the \"every edit registers\" rules in AGENTS.md (#4).\r\n> - Port order as a function of settings (#5).\r\n> \r\n> ### Temporary lines\r\n> - `apply(_:)` still rebuilds a node's ports, and `PortRegistry.register` and `remove` carry restore states. Both are replaced in #5.\r\n> \r\n> ### Note for merging\r\n> If `fix/string-split-separator` lands first, change its test's two `node.strategy = …` lines to `node.setStrategy(…)`.","files":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","additions":5,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"Fabric Editor/FabricApp.swift","additions":21,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"Fabric Editor/FabricDocument.swift","additions":14,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"